{"parentUuid":"e29f95c7-3648-42b7-99e4-bf5f224ffd91","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"insight-07","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01gDLdFmVYCcnQSsWx3AWMMd","content":"ledgerline/logging_setup.py:18:    handler = logging.FileHandler(settings.log_file)\nledgerline/settings.py:41:log_file = env(\"LEDGER_LOG_FILE\", \"/var/log/ledgerline/api.log\")"}]},"uuid":"f86d3ab2-a154-47a0-9327-833e94072ebb","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:41:50.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"f86d3ab2-a154-47a0-9327-833e94072ebb","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/ledgerline","sessionId":"insight-07","version":"2.0.14","gitBranch":"main","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_0100BrcafsFOxBeRCdF0xxVC","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the mechanism. The rule uses create mode: each night logrotate renames api.log to api.log.1 and creates a new, empty api.log. The api opened its log once with logging.FileHandler and keeps writing through that open file descriptor, so after the rename it writes into api.log.1. The next night delaycompress compresses api.log.1 into api.log.2.gz and deletes api.log.1, but the workers still hold it open, so the kernel cannot free the blocks. The deleted file keeps growing until the disk is full. Nothing ever tells the process to reopen its log.\n\nTwo fixes: restart the service now to free the space, and make the api reopen the file after rotation. Python has logging.handlers.WatchedFileHandler for exactly this: before each write it checks whether the file at the path is still the one it has open and reopens it if not. The other option is copytruncate in logrotate, but that can lose lines written between the copy and the truncate."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":435,"output_tokens":404}},"uuid":"ea708bdc-a869-475c-839c-2dca5ed1c14f","timestamp":"2026-09-16T07:41:53.000Z","requestId":"req_011ChJOuylxzOGve7Wy0UQ6w"}
